From: LYW-30M local development <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: stop on an invalid QMI memory segment count

The indication callback warns but still copies mem_seg_len entries into
fixed arrays. Return before changing mem_seg_count or touching either
array. This is a defensive bounds fix, not evidence that the current
firmware sends malformed segment counts.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -3146,9 +3146,11 @@
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_QMI, "firmware request memory request\n");
 
 	if (msg->mem_seg_len == 0 ||
-	    msg->mem_seg_len > ATH11K_QMI_WLANFW_MAX_NUM_MEM_SEG_V01)
+	    msg->mem_seg_len > ATH11K_QMI_WLANFW_MAX_NUM_MEM_SEG_V01) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "invalid memory segment length: %u\n",
 			    msg->mem_seg_len);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	ab->qmi.mem_seg_count = msg->mem_seg_len;
 
